# dependencies
node_modules/

# build output
dist/

# local env / editor noise
.env
.env.local
.DS_Store
*.log

# vercel
.vercel/

# claude code tooling + internal build brief (keep the public repo clean)
# The trailing /* matters: git will not re-include a path underneath an
# excluded DIRECTORY, so `.claude/` plus a negation silently ignores the skills
# anyway. Excluding the contents instead leaves the directory itself visible for
# the negation to work against.
.claude/*
# Skills are the exception, and they have to be committed to be worth anything:
# a web session clones this repo and sees only what git tracks, so an ignored
# skill is a skill that never loads. Nothing in there is private; it is the same
# method the site already describes out loud.
!.claude/skills/
fable5-build-prompt.md
